.TH "WEBTRANSPORTDATAGRAMSWRITABLE" "3JS" "September 1, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
WebTransportDatagramsWritable \- WebTransportDatagramsWritable
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]WebTransportDatagramsWritable\f[B]\f[R] interface of the
WebTransport API is a specialized \f[CR]WritableStream\f[R] that can be
used to write outgoing datagrams to a \f[CR]WebTransport\f[R]
connection.
.PP
\f[CR]WebTransportDatagramsWritable\f[R] is a transferable object.
.SH INSTANCE PROPERTIES
\f[I]Also inherits properties from its parent interface,
\f[CI]WritableStream\f[I].\f[R]
.TP
\f[B]WebTransportDatagramsWritable.sendGroup\f[R]
Gets or sets a \f[CR]WebTransportSendGroup\f[R] that the stream\(cqs
datagrams are grouped under for the purposes of \f[CR]sendOrder\f[R]
prioritization.
.TP
\f[B]WebTransportDatagramsWritable.sendOrder\f[R]
Gets or sets an integer indicating the priority of this stream relative
to other streams and datagrams in the same \f[CR]sendGroup\f[R].
.SH INSTANCE METHODS
\f[I]Inherits methods from its parent interface,
\f[CI]WritableStream\f[I].\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
In addition to the functionality of a standard
\f[CR]WritableStream\f[R], the \f[CR]WebTransportDatagramsWritable\f[R]
interface provides the \f[CR]sendGroup\f[R] property that indicates the
group of streams and datagrams that this stream belongs to, and the
\f[CR]sendOrder\f[R] property that indicates the relative priority of
this stream within that group.
Within a group, bytes queued on higher\-priority streams and datagrams
are sent before any bytes from lower\-priority ones.
Different groups are expected to be treated as equals for the purposes
of bandwidth allocation \(em though the precise way bandwidth is divided
between groups is implementation\-defined.
.PP
Objects of this type are not constructed directly.
Instead, an instance is returned by the \f[CR]createWritable()\f[R]
method of \f[CR]WebTransportDatagramDuplexStream\f[R], which can be
accessed using the \f[CR]WebTransport.datagrams\f[R] property.
.PP
The transmission is unreliable, meaning that even though you can define
the priority order, there is no guarantee that every datagram will be
sent, or that they will arrive in any particular order.
.SH EXAMPLES
See \f[CR]createWritable()\f[R] for an example showing how to create a
\f[CR]WebTransportDatagramsWritable\f[R] and use it to write outgoing
datagrams.
.SH SEE ALSO
